FILE: vUX-messageBox.js
FEATURE: message-box-module
DATE: 2026-10-09
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'modal-slide-effect' (uncommitted at the time)

REASON
NEW FILE. The MessageBox module: notification messages at the top of the window.

Design points worth recording:

  - Lanes. One position:fixed column per alignment (left/center/right) and offset,
    shared by every instance at module level, so two instances aligned the same way
    stack instead of overlapping. Below 600px every message uses the centre lane,
    because three full-width lanes would overlap.

  - Slots. Each message sits in a slot. The slot opens with
    $$.sm(slot).slide.toBottom() in dimension mode (no end size, so it opens to the
    content height) and closes with toTop(), so neighbours move aside smoothly.
    The core's .vSlide.dim class clips (overflow hidden), so the slot's overflow is
    set back to visible inline straight after the call. Otherwise a message
    travelling in from outside the slot would be hidden.

  - Effects use the core slide utility in position mode: drop = toBottom/toTop on
    "top"; slideLeft/slideRight = toLeft/toRight on "left" (never "right": an older
    cached core.css does not transition "right"). Every end of animation comes from
    the core's callback.

  - drop jumps to its start position (transition-property none + reflow) before
    toBottom. toBottom has no such step, and the message has just been measured, so
    it would otherwise transition from its resting place to the start and barely
    move. fade adds its class at build time for the same reason.

  - Exits aim 25% past the edge, because the core callback is a timer that can fire
    a frame before the transition ends (same finding as ModalDisplayer).

  - A close requested while a message is entering is deferred until it lands.
    Otherwise the slot's pending toBottom timer would set height:auto again and
    reopen a collapsing slot.

  - The timer counts from landing and pauses on hover/focus-within (remaining time
    kept), with the CSS countdown bar paused alongside.

  - Strings are set with textContent, never as markup.

  - Uses the core wherever it covers the job: $$.ce, $$.sm().class, $$.sm().slide,
    and the validateX/matchString helpers. The stylesheet is linked at import, as
    Skeleton's is, because linkStyleSheet waits 300ms.

